    title: 'How to Get Your First 100 Orders',
    subtitle: 'A tactical playbook for new Indian D2C brands — no ad budget required.',
    description: 'Step-by-step guide to getting your first 100 orders as a new Indian ecommerce brand using organic, WhatsApp, and community channels.',
    author: 'priya-commerce',
    publishedAt: '2026-05-15',
    updatedAt: '2026-06-15',
    tags: ['growth', 'beginners', 'organic', 'whatsapp'],
    readingTime: 10,
    featured: true,
    body: [
      { type: 'p', text: 'Your first 100 orders are the hardest. Not because the market is saturated — but because you have no social proof, no word-of-mouth, and no algorithm working for you yet. Everything is activation energy. This guide shows you how to build it.' },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'Why 100 Orders is the Magic Number' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'At 100 orders you have enough data to know: which products actually sell, what your real return rate is, which acquisition channel works for your brand, and what your unit economics look like at small scale. Everything before 100 is hypothesis. After 100, you\'re operating on evidence.' },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'Orders 1–10: Your Personal Network' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'Your first 10 orders should come from people who know you. Not because they\'re doing you a favor — but because getting them to pay full price validates that your positioning works. If people who like you won\'t pay for it, strangers definitely won\'t.' },
      { type: 'ul', items: ['Post on your personal Instagram and WhatsApp story with a real story behind the brand', 'Message 50 people personally (not a broadcast) — explain the product, ask for their honest opinion', 'Offer an early-supporter discount (15%) to the first 20 buyers — not a freebie, still paid', 'Ask every buyer to share a photo with the product on their stories'] },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'Orders 10–50: Community and WhatsApp Groups' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'India has the world\'s most active WhatsApp group ecosystem. Local resident welfare groups, college alumni chats, professional networks, hobby groups — all of them are potential buyers for the right product.' },
      { type: 'callout', variant: 'tip', title: 'WhatsApp Group Outreach', text: 'Don\'t post promotional messages directly. Instead, join relevant groups, contribute for 2–3 weeks, then share your product as "something I\'ve been working on." The warm intro approach gets 10x the engagement of cold promotion.' },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'Orders 50–100: Instagram Organic and Influencer Seeding' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'At 50 orders you have enough testimonials and product photos to build social proof. Use them to create Instagram content that answers questions your buyers had before purchasing. This becomes your content strategy.' },
      { type: 'ol', items: ['DM 50 micro-influencers (5K–50K followers) in your niche — offer free product, no paid contract', 'Post 3 times per week: 1 product post, 1 behind-the-scenes, 1 customer story', 'Use Instagram Stories daily — polls, questions, "swipe up" to your product', 'Reply to every comment within 2 hours for the first 3 months'] },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'Retain the First 100: The Thank You Advantage' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'Your first 100 buyers are your founding community. Treat them like it. A handwritten note in the package, a personal WhatsApp follow-up 5 days post-delivery, a referral incentive before they\'ve moved on — these are low-cost actions with outsized loyalty returns.' },
    ],
