    body: [
      { type: 'p', text: 'A non-compliant GST invoice can deny your buyer their input tax credit — and cost you their business. Getting invoicing right is a trust signal for B2B buyers and a legal requirement for all.' },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'Mandatory Fields on a GST Invoice' },
      { type: 'ul', items: ['Your business name, address, and GSTIN', 'Invoice number (consecutive, unique, reset yearly)', 'Invoice date', 'Buyer\'s name, address, and GSTIN (for B2B)', 'Place of supply (state)', 'HSN/SAC code for each item', 'Item description, quantity, and unit', 'Taxable value per item', 'GST rate (CGST+SGST for intra-state, IGST for inter-state)', 'GST amount per item and total', 'Total invoice amount in words'] },
      { type: 'callout', variant: 'info', title: 'LetBuyy Auto-Invoicing', text: 'LetBuyy generates fully GST-compliant invoices automatically for every order — with your GSTIN, HSN codes, correct CGST/SGST/IGST split, and sequential invoice numbers. Download, email, or WhatsApp to buyers in one click.' },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'HSN Codes: Getting Them Right' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'HSN (Harmonized System of Nomenclature) codes classify goods for GST purposes. Using the wrong HSN code means you\'ve applied the wrong tax rate. For apparel: 6101–6117. For footwear: 6401–6405. For electronics: 8501–8548. When in doubt, use the GST portal\'s HSN search tool.' },
      { type: 'h2', text: 'E-Invoice Mandate' },
      { type: 'p', text: 'If your annual turnover exceeds ₹5 crore, you must generate invoices through the GST e-invoice portal (IRP) and attach an IRN (Invoice Reference Number) and QR code. LetBuyy integrates with the IRP for merchants above this threshold.' },
    ],
